{
  "_comment": {
    "file": "Copy to money_rules.json and edit. Personal — never committed. Every key is optional: with no file at all the built-in rules still cover salary / bonus / interest, and every other counterparty shows up under `bin/money.sh review`.",
    "patterns": "Patterns are regular expressions. Each is tried against the normalized description and against the folded match key (small kana enlarged, long marks and spaces removed, billing-period suffixes like 「6月分」 stripped). A pattern with no regex metacharacters is folded the same way before matching, so you can write a name the way the world spells it even though the bank writes it with full-size kana.",
    "accounts": "Keys are the account ids the parsers produce. Rakuten Bank always reports as `rakuten_bank`; hand-maintained CSVs take their id from the filename up to the first `_` or `-` (mufg_2025-07.csv -> mufg). Labels are for display only.",
    "self_names": "Your own account holder name as it appears on transfers between your accounts, in katakana. Matching lines are treated as transfer candidates rather than income or spending.",
    "transfer_patterns": "Counterparties that move money rather than spend it, for the cases cross-account pairing cannot see because the other side is not imported — a brokerage, a time deposit, another bank.",
    "categories": "Evaluated top to bottom; the first match wins. These run before the built-in rules, so a specific counterparty can override a generic keyword. `label` is the display name for the whole category, so rules sharing a category should share a label — when they disagree the report falls back to the raw category key rather than labelling a combined total with one counterparty's name. `fixed_cost` and `note` are carried into the recurring-expense report in a later phase; `note` is for counterparties whose actual contents the statement never shows."
  },

  "accounts": {
    "rakuten_bank": { "label": "楽天銀行" },
    "mufg": { "label": "三菱UFJ銀行" }
  },

  "self_names": ["ヤマダ タロウ"],

  "transfer_patterns": ["ショウケンガイシャ", "テイキヨキン"],

